// String helpers that MBASIC/BASCOM 2.00 lack: ltrim$, rtrim$ and trim$. One
// require gets all three; `require com.bascal.stdlib.ltrim` (or rtrim) still
// works on its own, and requiring both never declares anything twice. See
// ltrim.bcl and rtrim.bcl for why these are scalar methods.
library strings

require com.bascal.stdlib.ltrim
require com.bascal.stdlib.rtrim

method trim[string]()
    return ltrim$(rtrim$(self$))
end method
